<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kaan</h1><p class="st-meta">400 CE – 900 CE (approx.) · capital Calakmul</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Snake Kingdom, the most powerful Classic Maya state, which from Dzibanche and later Calakmul built a network of allies to encircle Tikal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The snake-head emblem dynasty of Kaan is first firmly attested at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzibanche">Dzibanche</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a> in the 5th and 6th centuries. Around 635 the dynasty moved its seat to Calakmul in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, a large city whose own earlier lords had used a different emblem.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kaan exercised power through hegemony rather than direct rule: subject kings at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caracol">Caracol</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naranjo">Naranjo</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dos-pilas">Dos Pilas</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/el-peru-waka">El Perú-Waka'</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/la-corona">La Corona</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cancuen">Cancuén</a> acknowledged its overlords. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuknoom-cheen-ii">Yuknoom Ch'een II</a>, who reigned from 636 to about 686, it reached its height, and Calakmul holds more stelae than any other Maya city. Its alliance defeated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tikal">Tikal</a> in 562.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tikal's victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuknoom-yichaak-kahk">Yuknoom Yich'aak K'ahk'</a> in 695 broke Kaan's dominance, and its network fragmented in the 8th century. Calakmul raised its last monuments around 900. The kingdom remained little known until its glyphs were deciphered in the 1990s.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 400 CE – 900 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/